get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{27}{x} & =9 \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{27}{x} & =x\\cdot 9 \\\\ \\cancel{x}\\cdot \\frac{27}{\\cancel{x}} & =9x \\\\ 27 & =9x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27 & =9x \\\\ \\frac{27}{9} & =\\frac{9x}{9} \\\\ 3 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=3$ is different from $x=0$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491999 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491999 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216726" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491999 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491999 #edb/ref 1071 "The solution to $\\frac{7x+4}{2x-1}=5$ is$\\,\\,x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491999 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1b74041d-b56d-586f-9721-4bae2781f6fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491999 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by the denominator $(2x-1)$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x+4}{2x-1} & =5 \\\\ (2x-1)\\cdot \\frac{7x+4}{2x-1} & =(2x-1)\\cdot 5 \\\\ \\cancel{(2x-1)}\\cdot \\frac{7x+4}{\\cancel{2x-1}} & =(2x-1)\\cdot 5 \\\\ 7x+4 & =10x-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+4 & =10x-5 \\\\ 7x+4+5 & =10x-5+5 \\\\ 7x+9 & =10x \\\\ 7x+9-7x & =10x-7x \\\\ 9 & =3x \\\\ \\frac{9}{3} & =\\frac{3x}{3} \\\\ 3 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=3$ is different from $x=\\frac{1}{2}$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492020 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492020 #edb/ref 1069 "q-212105" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492020 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492020 #edb/ref 1071 "The solution to $\\frac{12}{x}=3$ is$\\,\\,x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492020 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5f04aac8-e6e7-5764-9921-97e34f5f1880" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492020 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=0$ cannot be a solution. This is because if $x=0,$ then the rational term would be $\\frac{12}{0},$ which is undefined because it has a zero denominator.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by the denominator $x$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{x} & =3 \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{12}{x} & =x\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\cancel{x}\\cdot \\frac{12}{\\cancel{x}} & =3x \\\\ 12 & =3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =3x \\\\ \\frac{12}{3} & =\\frac{3x}{3} \\\\ 4 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=4$ is different from $x=0$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492022 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492022 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216650" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492022 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492022 #edb/ref 1071 "The solution to $2=\\frac{6x}{x+10}$ is$\\,\\,x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492022 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "695f0f45-ca26-5a8e-af61-5e5eccb763aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492022 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=-10$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by the denominator $(x+10)$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{6x}{x+10} \\\\ (x+10)\\cdot 2 & =(x+10)\\cdot \\frac{6x}{x+10} \\\\ (x+10)\\cdot 2 & =\\cancel{(x+10)}\\cdot \\frac{6x}{\\cancel{x+10}} \\\\ 2x+20 & =6x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+20 & =6x \\\\ 2x+20-2x & =6x-2x \\\\ 20 & =4x \\\\ \\frac{20}{4} & =\\frac{4x}{4} \\\\ 5 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $x=5$ is different from $x=-10$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492027 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492027 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216629" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492027 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492027 #edb/ref 1071 "The solution to $14=\\frac{7}{x}$ is$\\,\\,x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492027 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "74bd71aa-77f2-5627-a97e-2a16e71261b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492027 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=0$ cannot be a solution. This is because if $x=0,$ then the rational term would be $\\frac{7}{0},$ which is undefined because it has a zero denominator.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by the denominator $x$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & =\\frac{7}{x} \\\\ x\\cdot 14 & =x\\cdot \\frac{7}{x} \\\\ x\\cdot 14 & =\\cancel{x}\\cdot \\frac{7}{\\cancel{x}} \\\\ 14x & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14x & =7 \\\\ \\frac{14x}{14} & =\\frac{7}{14} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ is different from $x=0$, we can accept it as a solution.  Thus, the solution is $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492042 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492042 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216636" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492042 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492042 #edb/ref 1071 "The solution to $\\frac{9}{2x}=3$ is$\\,\\,x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492042 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a6a33051-a015-5020-a25d-850890a866df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492042 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=0$ cannot be a solution. This is because if $x=0,$ then the rational term would be $\\frac{9}{2\\cdot 0},$ which is undefined because it has a zero denominator.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by $(2x)$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2x} & =3 \\\\ 2x\\cdot \\frac{9}{2x} & =3\\cdot 2x \\\\ \\cancel{2x}\\cdot \\frac{9}{\\cancel{2x}} & =6x \\\\ 9 & =6x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =6x \\\\ \\frac{9}{6} & =\\frac{6x}{6} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ is different from $x=0$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=\\frac{3}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492047 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492047 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216906" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492047 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492047 #edb/ref 1071 "The solution to $\\frac{8}{3x-2}=2$ is$\\,\\,x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492047 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2a4b507-db6c-548d-8dc8-8ead746b1a3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492047 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=\\frac{2}{3}$ is an excluded solution since division by $0$ is undefined.  \n\nTo solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by the denominator $(3x-2)$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3x-2} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{8(3x-2)}{(3x-2)} & =2(3x-2) \\\\ \\frac{8\\cancel{(3x-2)}}{\\cancel{(3x-2)}} & =2(3x-2) \\\\ 8 & =6x-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =6x-4 \\\\ 8+4 & =6x-4+4 \\\\ 12 & =6x \\\\ \\frac{12}{6} & =\\frac{6x}{6} \\\\ 2 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $x=2$ is different from $x=\\frac{2}{3}$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492059 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491920 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492059 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216640" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492059 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492059 #edb/ref 1071 "The solution to $\\frac{6x}{x+4}=3$ is$\\,\\,x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492059 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf8fa259-5b82-5b77-ac27-d9afdcd671e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492059 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=-4$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by the denominator $(x+4)$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x}{x+4} & =3 \\\\ (x+4)\\cdot \\frac{6x}{x+4} & =(x+4)\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\cancel{(x+4)}\\cdot \\frac{6x}{\\cancel{x+4}} & =(x+4)\\cdot 3 \\\\ 6x & =3x+12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & =3x+12 \\\\ 6x-3x & =3x+12-3x \\\\ 3x & =12 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & =\\frac{12}{3} \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=4$ is different from $x=-4$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492070 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492070 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216627" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492070 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492070 #edb/ref 1071 "The solution to $\\frac{16}{x}=8$ is$\\,\\,x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492070 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f69af0e1-99d0-5dff-a9e0-4071bc340c80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492070 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=0$ cannot be a solution. This is because if $x=0,$ then the rational term would be $\\frac{16}{0},$ which is undefined because it has a zero denominator.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by the denominator $x$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16}{x} & =8 \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{16}{x} & =x\\cdot 8 \\\\ \\cancel{x}\\cdot \\frac{16}{\\cancel{x}} & =8x \\\\ 16 & =8x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16 & =8x \\\\ \\frac{16}{8} & =\\frac{8x}{8} \\\\ 2 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ is different from $x=0$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
